# Append-only files: concurrent sessions add entries at the same place,
# so every parallel promotion conflicts on them and the resolution is
# always "keep both". Git's built-in union driver does exactly that,
# with no per-clone configuration.
#
# Deliberately NOT applied to wiki/_views/** — those are generated, and
# merging them line by line would corrupt them. The `rebase` skill
# resolves views by re-running `brain.py views` (byte-identical to
# `tabula index`), which is deterministic against the merged tree and
# therefore the correct resolution.
#
# The tradeoff union accepts: two sessions editing the *same existing*
# line produce both versions silently instead of a conflict. That is
# visible in review and cheap to fix, unlike the alternative it replaces
# (hand-resolving the same union on every promotion, where the risk is a
# mis-resolution that drops someone's entry).

log/log.md      merge=union
wiki/index.md   merge=union
